# ESM1.6 Output Postprocessing Cylc Suite

This suite is intended to be used to post-process data output from ESM1.6 that
was created before the changes to follow the ACCESS Ouutput Data Specifications
were integrated with the ESM1.6 workflows (i.e. before August 2026).
This suite is intended to be run on NCI's Gadi.

## Running the Suite

If one is new to cylc please follow the [instructions](https://opus.nci.org.au/spaces/DAE/pages/338002344/Cylc+Getting+Started+Guide+for+New+User) provided by NCI.

### Postprocessing One Dataset

To postprocess a single data update `rose-suite.conf` with the path to the dataset and run the suite as normal:
```bash
esm1p6_postprocessor $ cylc install .
esm1p6_postprocessor $ cylc play esm1p6_postprocessor
```

If the data is not in the expected location then the `STORAGE` flags in `rose-suite.conf` will need to be updated.

### Postprocessing Many Datasets
The `lauch_suite.sh` script can be used to launch multiple cylc workflows to postprocess multiple datasets at once.
To use this script update the `DATASET_LIST` variable with the paths to the datasets in question.
Wildcards can be used in these paths and the script will look for a `output000` in each matched path to confirm it's a dataset before launching the postprocessing suite.

E.g. postprocess all the datasets under `/g/data/p73/archive/CMIP7/ACCESS-ESM1-6/production/` and `/g/data/p73/archive/CMIP7/ACCESS-ESM1-6/development/`:
```bash
DATASET_LIST=(
    "/g/data/p73/archive/CMIP7/ACCESS-ESM1-6/production/*"
    "/g/data/p73/archive/CMIP7/ACCESS-ESM1-6/development/*"
)
```
Any non-dataset directorys that match the wildcard should be ignored.

## Options

### Normal Mode

By default this suite will output postprocessed files to the same location as the original dataset.
The original files will be archived under `$DATASET_DIR/output???/$REALM/old_data_archive` unless `DELETE_OLD_DATA` is set to `True` in `rose-suite.conf`.

### Scratch Mode
To output to another location (i.e. scratch) set `SCRATCH_MODE = True` and `SCRATCH_DIR` to the desired output location in `rose-suite.conf`.
In this mode the files in the original location will not be changed in any way.
